          },
          "code": "ANALYZERLLM",
          "id": "1771267800792",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771267800793_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Quality report analyst for Product/Items reported quality problems/issues.\n\nUse data context as your knowledge: \n {{$context.$nodes.GETPROBLEMREPORTFORITEM.$output}}\n \nUser Query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nGenerate reply based on user question: \n\nAnalyze potential issues and severity , create summary details. Do not ask questions.\nAlways Generate a Short and Concise Summary in Bullet points on top of the display outcome:\n- Produce a concise executive summary\n- Actions and Recommendations\n\n**Do Not generate any action insights**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateChart"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATECHART",
          "id": "1771535461776",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771535461778_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Follow Instruction: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nUse data context as your knowledge: \n {{$context.$nodes.GETPROBLEMREPORTFORITEM.$output}}\n \nAnalyze , identify and capture\n- Produce a concise executive summary\n- Risks\n- Quality specific Recommendations\n\nYou must ALWAYS produce BOTH of the following in your response, in this exact order:\n\n1. A comprehensive quality summary report in __valid HTML__, which MUST appear __before__ any `<oraInfoDisplay/>` node.\n2. An `<oraInfoDisplay/>` node that contains only the display configuration for table/graph widgets.\n\nHard requirements:\n\n- The HTML summary must be OUTSIDE of `<oraInfoDisplay/>` (never nested inside it).\n- The HTML summary must be a complete HTML fragment (e.g., `<html><body>...</body></html>` or at least `<div>...</div>`).\n- The `<oraInfoDisplay/>` node MUST NOT contain the quality summary text.\n\nUse this output skeleton and fill in the details:\n\n<html> <body> <!-- Quality summary content here --> </body> </html><oraInfoDisplay> <!-- Widget configuration here --> </oraInfoDisplay>\n\nNow fill in `<HtmlSummary>` and `<oraInfoDisplay>` with appropriate content.\n\nGenerate a comprehensive quality summary report in HTML format. The report should include the following sections followed strictly:\n<strong>Executive Summary</strong>\n<Executive summary Details> in a bullet format.\n<strong>Risks</strong>\n<Risks Details> in a bullet format.\n<strong>Recommendations</strong>\n<Quality specific Recommendations> in a bullet format.\n\nGenerate multiRecordWidget <oraInfoDisplay> node using data context.\n\n**Do Not generate any action insights**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
